# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Lumen OS on the XGIMI Z9X HB (goat_elegant, G0130), test builds from t8c on: two vendor services that can never
# link on this model are not left in init's 5 s restart loop (installed as /system/etc/init/hb_vendor_services.rc by
# compose_hb.sh; HB only, no other device stages this file, the Z9X and Play 6 images do not change).
#
# Evidence (T8_NOTES.md, T8C_NOTES.md):
# - /vendor/etc/init/hw/init.xgimi.gmpf.rc defines "service smart_ak_server /vendor/bin/smart_ak_server" and
#   "service infoDisp_server /vendor/bin/infoDisp_server", both class main, disabled, user root, not oneshot.
# - Both binaries NEED libirseg.so, which does not export _ZN2cv3ocl17isOpenCLActivatedEv; no other library of the
#   NEEDED tree, of the stock vendor or of the stock system defines it. So the dynamic linker gives up before main:
#   'cannot locate symbol "_ZN2cv3ocl17isOpenCLActivatedEv"' (hb-t7 log, T7_NOTES.md A6). The same on the stock
#   HB firmware: XGIMI switched the feature off for G0130 (vendor/etc/xgimimodelname/G0130/build.prop:44,
#   "# persist.vendor.xgimi.smart_ak_server=1"), the stock getprop dump has no init.svc.smart_ak_server.
# - The gmpf HAL (libxgimi.so) sends ctl.start smart_ak_server for the smart AK steps and ctl.stop after
#   smartFinish; after a failed start it does not send ctl.stop, so init restarts the service every 5 s until a
#   reboot (hb-t7 after Auto keystone / Fit to screen: the linker error every 5 s).
# - On the owner's Z9X (64-bit vendor) the same services link and stop normally. This file is not on the Z9X.
#
# What the triggers do: init sets init.svc.NAME=restarting only when a non-oneshot service exited ON ITS OWN and
# init has scheduled the restart. "stop" then clears the pending restart and sets init.svc.NAME=stopped. So:
# - a successful run is never touched: the HAL's ctl.stop goes running -> stopping -> stopped, never restarting;
# - the next ctl.start of the HAL starts the service again as before (stop does not disable it for good), so each
#   AK run gives one link failure in the log instead of one every 5 s forever;
# - the HAL path is the same as now: the process dies in the linker before main in both cases, never reports a
#   status, and the HAL's own wait ends on its timeout ("wait alg status time out!") as it does today. Only the
#   respawns after that are gone.
# Init builtin only, no vendor file is changed. A service name the vendor lacks would only log an init error.
on property:init.svc.smart_ak_server=restarting
    stop smart_ak_server

on property:init.svc.infoDisp_server=restarting
    stop infoDisp_server
